{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "godunov_norm_1d_periodic_exact",
    "description": "Exactness driver for grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/godunov_norm_D1_periodic on the periodic unit interval [0,1] at N=64: the first-order Godunov (Rouy-Tourin / Osher-Sethian) gradient magnitude ANNIHILATES a spatially constant field EXACTLY, the null-space mimetic property |grad(const)| = 0 (the low-order 1-D cartesian analogue of the grad(const) = 0 gate in problems/gradient_mpas.esm). The state holds a constant field u(x) = 3, evolved under the Hamilton-Jacobi step u_t = -S|u_x| discretized as u_t = -S*godunov(u); with u constant every backward and forward difference is a subtraction of equal floats (u[i]-u[i-1] = 3-3 = 0.0 to the bit, at the interior AND at the two periodic-wrap faces u[1]-u[N] = u[N+1=1]-u[N] = 0.0), so sqrt(max(0,0)^2 + min(0,0)^2) = 0 EXACTLY at every cell, du/dt = 0.0 to the bit, and u(t) = u(0) = 3 for all time with NO rounding drift (a constant difference is an exact zero, not an O(eps) residual). The gate asserts the preserved state directly: L2_error of u versus the constant reference 3 is 0 at t=0 and t=1 (within 1e-13), and mean(u) = 3 (within 1e-13). Because this is a STATE assertion (the binding evaluates reductions of the state solution, and analytic build-time references, but cannot evaluate an observed that reads the state), it is the sim-expressible exactness deliverable. The stronger interior property that the Godunov norm reproduces |u_x| = |a| EXACTLY for a NON-constant affine field u = a x + b (interior D- = D+ = a, so sqrt(max(a,0)^2 + min(a,0)^2) = |a| with no truncation error) is NOT expressible as a periodic simulation gate: a non-constant ramp cannot be periodic, so its two wrap faces are seam artifacts that a state reduction cannot exempt, and the binding cannot assert a face-masking observed of the state. That interior exactness is pinned instead by the AST golden (tests/conformance/ast/godunov_norm_D1_periodic, the correct max/min stencil structure) and is exercised on nontrivial data by the order-1 convergence sweep problems/godunov_norm_1d_eikonal_mms.esm, whose clean first-order error confirms the entropy fix selects the exact one-sided branch. The grid's consumer-supplied geometry contract (grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm) is fulfilled for [0,1]: x0 = 0 and dx = 1/N (an observed dividing the extent by the metaparameter name N, esm-spec 9.7.6). The constant field needs no coordinate geometry, so the ic and reference evaluations stay build-time scope-free.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_1d",
      "equation:hamilton_jacobi",
      "exactness"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Osher, S., & Sethian, J. A. (1988). Fronts propagating with curvature-dependent speed: Algorithms based on Hamilton-Jacobi formulations. Journal of Computational Physics, 79(1), 12-49. The Godunov |grad phi| upwind construction, whose max/min differences vanish on a constant field.",
        "doi": "10.1016/0021-9991(88)90002-2"
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "GodunovNormExact": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/godunov_norm_D1_periodic.esm"
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Constant level-set field u(x) = 3; the Godunov norm annihilates it, so u_t = -S*godunov(u) = 0 and u holds its ic for all time."
        },
        "S": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/s",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Non-negative Hamilton-Jacobi speed (u_t = -S|u_x|); any value leaves u fixed since |u_x| = 0 for the constant field."
        },
        "x0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Left domain edge a = 0 (unit interval): the grid's x0 free name (consumer-supplied geometry contract, grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm)."
        },
        "dx": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Grid spacing (b - a)/N = 1/N: the grid's dx free name, resolved inside the rewrite rule's expanded body at evaluation. N is the document-scoped metaparameter, substituted as an integer literal at load (esm-spec 9.7.6)."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "ic",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ]
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "i"
            ],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "i": {
                "from": "x"
              }
            },
            "expr": 3.0
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ],
            "wrt": "t"
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  "S"
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "sqrt",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "^",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "D",
                        "args": [
                          "u"
                        ],
                        "wrt": "x"
                      },
                      2
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "dx",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              1,
              "N"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "constant_field_annihilated_exact",
          "description": "The Godunov gradient magnitude annihilates a constant field to the bit (|grad(const)| = 0), so the constant state is preserved exactly. Derivation: u(i) = 3 for every cell, so every backward difference u[i]-u[i-1] and forward difference u[i+1]-u[i] — interior AND the periodic-wrap faces (u[1]-u[N], u[1]-u[N]) — is 3.0 - 3.0 = 0.0 exactly, and sqrt(max(0,0)^2 + min(0,0)^2) = 0.0; hence u_t = -S*0 = 0.0 to the bit and u(t) = 3 for all t with no drift. The L2_error assertions pin u to the constant reference 3 at t=0 (ic wiring) and t=1 (preservation under the lowered operator) within 1e-13, and mean(u) = 3 confirms independently. Any lowering or evaluation defect in the max/min/sqrt makearray (a surviving unlowered D, a broken face region, a sign error) that produced a nonzero |grad| on the constant field would drive u off 3 by O(S t) and blow past the 1e-13 tolerance by orders of magnitude. Because a constant difference is an exact float zero, the tolerance could be 0; 1e-13 leaves headroom for the solver's own arithmetic.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 1.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 1e-13
              },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "aggregate",
                "output_idx": [
                  "i"
                ],
                "args": [],
                "ranges": {
                  "i": {
                    "from": "x"
                  }
                },
                "expr": 3.0
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 1.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 1e-13
              },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "aggregate",
                "output_idx": [
                  "i"
                ],
                "args": [],
                "ranges": {
                  "i": {
                    "from": "x"
                  }
                },
                "expr": 3.0
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 1.0,
              "expected": 3.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 1e-13
              },
              "reduce": "mean"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
